{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And in your land you shall not do.</b> Since above he mentioned ומעוך, and that is the castrated one, therefore Scripture juxtaposed ובארצכם לא תעשו — you shall not do thus, to castrate any living creature, even unclean. And when it says 'in your land,' it is not to say that we were commanded only in the land — for castration is an obligation of the body in every place — but it comes only to include everything that is in your land, even unclean things, that you shall not castrate them. Or the word תעשו may mean the opposite of making, that is, the nullification of generation; and like it (Ecclesiastes 9:5): ״כי אינם יודעים לעשות רע״ — that is, to nullify evil and remove it; and likewise (Genesis 9:24): ״אשר עשה לו בנו הקטן״, which the rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted as 'he castrated him.' And from this, in my opinion, is (Proverbs 6:32): ״משחית נפשו הוא יעשנה״ — for the one who sins in adultery destroys his soul, and whoever destroys his soul certainly nullifies it and removes it from its proper level, for it is not in man's power to make the soul, but it is in his power to destroy it and nullify it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:39.841854427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}